comment0.target=Wheel
comment0.text=\r\n Represents a single wheel of the slot machine.\r\n Each wheel owns its own list of symbols and its visual \r\n representation\: a background Rectangle (slot) and a Traingle\r\n that shows the currently visible symbol (visibleShape). Both\r\n shapes are created once, with a fixed size; only their color changes when the wheel spins\r\n \r\n @author Oscar Poveda, Elian Ibarra\r\n @version 1.0\r\n
comment1.params=posX posY
comment1.target=Wheel(int, int)
comment1.text=\r\n Constructs the object for every wheel of the board\r\n @param posX the position in X axis of the board\r\n @param posY the position in Y axis of the board\r\n
comment10.target=void refreshShape()
comment10.text=\r\n Updates the color of the visible shape on the screen\r\n according to the symbol that is located on the \r\n current index\r\n
comment11.params=newPosX newPosY
comment11.target=void accommodate(int, int)
comment11.text=\r\n Repositions the slot and its associated visual shape on the canvas based on grid coordinates.\r\n Translates the grid matrix positions into screen pixel coordinates using the cell size, \r\n gap spacing, and offset adjustments, then updates the internal position state.\r\n @param newPosX the target column (X index) in the grid matrix\r\n @param newPosY the target row (Y index) in the grid matrix\r\n
comment12.params=move
comment12.target=void accommodate(int)
comment12.text=\r\n Moves this wheel one grid position forward (move \=\= 1) or\r\n backward (move \=\= -1), wrapping to the next/previous row\r\n when it falls off the edge of the grid. Delegates to\r\n accommodate(int, int) with the newly computed position.\r\n
comment13.target=void pause()
comment14.params=distance
comment14.target=void slowMoveHorizontal(int)
comment15.params=distance
comment15.target=void slowMoveVertical(int)
comment16.params=symbol
comment16.target=int getIndexOfSymbol(java.lang.String)
comment16.text=\r\n Returns the index of the symbol on the array according to its value\r\n @param symbol string value of the symbol\r\n
comment17.params=posX posY
comment17.target=void setLocation(int, int)
comment17.text=\r\n Modify the coordiinates of the wheel to the new values\r\n @param posX the new position in X axis of the board\r\n @param posY the new position in Y axis of the board\r\n
comment18.target=void lock()
comment18.text=\r\n Locks this wheel, preventing it from being spun or modified\r\n until it is explicitly unlocked.\r\n
comment19.target=void unlock()
comment19.text=\r\n Unlocks this wheel, allowing it to be spun or modified again.\r\n
comment2.params=index
comment2.target=void addSymbol(int)
comment2.text=\r\n Adds a symbol to the wheel's visible cycle, adjusting the current\r\n index if the new symbol was inserted before or at the wheel's\r\n current position.\r\n @param index 1-based position at which the new symbol was inserted\r\n              into the global symbols list\r\n
comment20.target=boolean isLocked()
comment20.text=\r\n Returns whether this element is currently locked.\r\n\r\n @return true if locked, false otherwise\r\n
comment3.params=color
comment3.target=void delSymbol(java.lang.String)
comment3.text=\r\n Removes a symbol to the symbols array for all\r\n the wheels of the board\r\n @param color string value of the symbol's color\r\n
comment4.params=color
comment4.target=void placeSymbol(java.lang.String)
comment4.text=\r\n Updates the value of the index of the current wheel\r\n @param color string value of the symbol's color\r\n
comment5.params=direction
comment5.target=void spin(int)
comment5.text=\r\n Changes the wheel's visible symbol by one position in the given\r\n direction\: forward (direction \=\= 1) advances to the next symbol,\r\n wrapping to the first when at the end; backward (direction \=\= -1)\r\n moves to the previous symbol, wrapping to the last when at the start.\r\n\r\n @param direction 1 to advance one step, -1 to go back one step\r\n
comment6.target=void spin()
comment6.text=\r\n Change the wheel ("spin" the board) going to the next one on the slot.\r\n Equivalent to spin(1).\r\n
comment7.target=java.lang.String visibleSymbol()
comment7.text=\r\n Return the symbol located on the current index\r\n
comment8.target=void makeVisible()
comment8.text=\r\n Show the wheel\: the symbol and the slot which it\r\n is located\r\n
comment9.target=void makeInvisible()
comment9.text=\r\n Hide the wheel\: the symbol and the slot which it\r\n is located\r\n
